-- title:
--   Rational endomorphism subring is invariant under variable change
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, let $X$ and $Y$ be Weierstrass curves over $k$, and let $C$ be a Weierstrass variable change over $k$ (a quadruple $(u,r,s,t)$ with $u$ invertible) such that $C \cdot X = Y$. For a Weierstrass curve $W$ over $k$, write $(W⁄k)$ for its base change to $k$ with its affine model, and let $\mathrm{rationalEndSubring}\ k\ W$ be the subring of $\mathrm{End}_{+}((W⁄k)(k))$ generated by those additive endomorphisms $\alpha$ of the group of points that are either zero or satisfy the predicate `IsRationallyRepresented k W W`. The assertion is that there is a ring isomorphism $\varphi : \mathrm{rationalEndSubring}\ k\ X \xrightarrow{\sim} \mathrm{rationalEndSubring}\ k\ Y$ which is conjugation by the change-of-variables bijection: writing $e : (Y⁄k)(k) \to (X⁄k)(k)$ for the bijection `equivOfVariableChangeEq hC` attached to the equality $C \cdot X = Y$, one has, for every $\alpha$ in $\mathrm{rationalEndSubring}\ k\ X$ and every point $P$ of $(Y⁄k)$, the identity $(\varphi\,\alpha)(P) = e^{-1}(\alpha(e(P)))$, where $\alpha$ and $\varphi\,\alpha$ are regarded as additive endomorphisms of the respective point groups. Only the existence of such a $\varphi$ is asserted, not a named construction.
--
--   This records that an admissible change of Weierstrass coordinates induces an isomorphism of the rings of rationally represented endomorphisms, the transport being conjugation by the induced bijection on points. It is used in the construction of a model of a curve over a subfield together with the identification of the Frobenius action on its endomorphism subring, in [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_subfield_model_frobenius_eq_smul_rationalEndSubring_equiv`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_subfield_model_frobenius_eq_smul_rationalEndSubring_equiv).
